#################################################################
#  COVERAGE GAP — what this file deliberately does not cover
#################################################################

cvg:vcguk3N7G4YK13FxzhYYpa
    a mrs:CoverageGap ;
    mrs:gapScope mrs:gs_person_class ;
    mrs:gapDescription "This file adds ~100 incidents spanning the full Prophetic era and the Rashidun succession, compiled directly by the project maintainer as seed material rather than through independent AI research (see file header). It is not scholar-reviewed, not matched to specific source passages or editions, and its approximate CE datings are conventional, not calendar-precise. Several named groups mentioned in the source incidents (the Ansar as a body, the Quraysh delegation to Abyssinia, the confederate tribes at the Trench) are referenced only generically and are not individually modelled. This is exactly the material the step-by-step roadmap ('The Road Ahead') describes as needing a real review workbench and real historians before any of it can be marked verified."@en ;
    mrs:gapCause mrs:gc_not_yet_ingested ;
    mrs:knownSource "The user's own 100-incident seed compilation, September 2026 (see project chat log); standard sira/maghazi/futuh secondary literature for eventual source-matching."@en .

# Linked to the origin Person (generation-1.ttl's Prophet IRI) so it is
# discoverable the same way generation-1.ttl's own CoverageGap (linked to
# the Badr Event) already is -- an unlinked CoverageGap validates under
# CoverageGapShape but is otherwise an orphan no query can find.
per:2mQ7vR9nK4pT8sY3wZ6xCe mrs:coverageGap cvg:vcguk3N7G4YK13FxzhYYpa .
